# Diagnostic authority

These four rules override convenience. Do not violate them.

## 1. AI owns semantics

The diagnostic model interprets free-form mechanic text (complaint, result, confirmation).
The backend does not infer meaning from that prose, except a minimal deterministic legacy fail-safe when a stored observation has no typed intent.

```ts
// BAD — backend decides the mechanic confirmed a fault
if (/potvrđeno|to je to|riješeno/i.test(resultText)) actionType = "FINISH";

// GOOD — model returns technicianOutcome; backend only type-checks the enum
turn.technicianOutcome = parseTechnicianOutcome(draft.semanticUpdate?.technicianOutcome) ?? null;
```

## 2. Backend owns structure and invariants

State, enums, evidence provenance, retry limits, and safety/spec guards stay in the backend.
The backend validates types, merges case facts, and rejects drafts that break invariants.
It does not rewrite ASK/TEST into FINISH or invent confirmedFault, rationale, or confidence.

## 3. Internal control flow uses typed codes

Never branch on your own issue or error strings (`startsWith`, `includes`, regex).

```ts
// BAD
if (issue.startsWith("TECHNICIAN OUTCOME")) { ... }
if (/ASK REJECT/i.test(issue)) { ... }

// GOOD
if (issue.code === "TECHNICIAN_OUTCOME") { ... }
if (issue.code === "ASK_REJECT") { ... }
```

Set `code` where the issue is created. `message` is for the model and logs only.

## 4. UI intent is structured

A button click sends an intent enum. Do not turn a click into a fake free-text observation that the backend then parses.

```ts
// BAD
onSkip={() => continue("Preskočeno za sada.")}
onReject={() => continue("TECHNICIAN_REJECTED_DIAGNOSIS: ...")}

// GOOD
onSkip={() => continue({ intent: "SKIP" })}
onReject={() => continue({ intent: "REJECT_DIAGNOSIS" })}
```

`SUBMIT_RESULT` is the only intent that carries mechanic prose. The model interprets that prose.
